# Narrow allowlist-style ignores. Anything not on this list MUST be
# tracked. If you find yourself wanting to add an entry, ask the user
# explicitly first — silently excluding data files is the failure mode
# this discipline exists to prevent.

# Python build / cache artifacts (regeneratable from source)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Virtualenvs (regeneratable; the lockfile/requirements is what matters)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor scratch (NOT data files — those go in git)
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Explicitly NOT ignored — kept here as a manifest of what we
# deliberately commit even though tooling might suggest otherwise:
#
#   data/        # candidates, inbox, all analytical inputs
#   output/      # generated screens and portfolio reports
#   src/         # the pipeline code
#   *.md         # all documentation and analytical write-ups
#   .claude/     # session-start hooks and project settings
#   Makefile     # the workflow entrypoints
#
# If you ever feel tempted to add data/, output/, .cache/, or any
# directory whose contents represent expensive fetched state to this
# file, STOP. That is exactly the durability hole that destroyed the
# prior session's work.
